            <ArticleTitle>[Pain syndrome in cancer patients after lung and breast surgery].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>41-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Analysing, the results of questionnaires offered to cancer patients on days 1 and 2 after lung (50 males) and mammalian (50 females) surgery more detailed clinical structures of acute pain syndrome have been identified. Different pain syndromes develop after intra- and extrathoracic surgery. They are characterized by distinct intensity, maximum pain onset, pain irradiation and concomitant events. The detailed clinical structure of these acute pain syndromes described allowed of a more directed effective antinociceptive therapy establishing &quot;analgetic comfort&quot; in the postoperative period.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
